{{!--
  Source repo link in the header toolbar (see GH issue #7). Resolved from site
  or component configuration, never a literal: `site.keys.repoUrl` is the
  playbook-level override (see antora-playbook.yml's `asciidoc.attributes` /
  `site.keys` — set under `site.keys.repo_url`); `page.origin.webUrl` is what
  Antora derives per-component from the content source's git remote when no
  override is given. Renders nothing, not a dead "#" link, when neither exists.

  GH-77: icon-only, GitHub's own mark rather than the generic external-link
  glyph — same `--icon-mask-brand-github` custom property cta.js's own GitHub
  action already defines (cta.css), reused here rather than duplicated.
  Icon-only needs the accessible name on the link itself (no visible label
  left), same convention as search-fab__trigger.
--}}
{{#with (or site.keys.repoUrl page.origin.webUrl)}}
<a class="ids-button ids-button--ghost ids-button--icon-only header-toolbar__repo" href="{{{this}}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Repository">
  <span class="ids-button__content">
    <span class="ids-button__icon ids-button__icon-icon header-toolbar__repo-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </span>
</a>
{{/with}}
